      ⍝ complex columns p. 17-18 ----------------------------------
      ⍝
      ⍝ The real parts and the imaginary parts of a column are formatted
      ⍝ as two sub-columns, each in the same format (scaled as a whole if
      ⍝ one item needs it, same number of fractional digits). The J's are
      ⍝ aligned, but unlike in the LRM example on p. 18 (2   J3, which
      ⍝ also aligns the decimal points of the real parts) without blanks
      ⍝ inside a number: the real part is directly left and the imaginary
      ⍝ part directly right of the J. A column without any J is aligned
      ⍝ like a real column.
      ⍝
      2 4⍴1 12.3 345 6J7 .1 .12 1J2 16J6
1   12.3  345    6J7
0.1  0.12   1J2 16J6



      4 4⍴0 1 2J3 4J5.6 7.8J9
  0       1       2J3 4J5.6
7.8J9     0       1   2J3
  4J5.6 7.8J9     0   1
  2J3     4J5.6 7.8J9 0



