      ⍝ columns of mixed and nested arrays ----------------------------
      ⍝
      ⍝ As in IBM APL2, the numbers in a column of a mixed or nested array
      ⍝ have no common format (e.g. 600.0E0). Unlike IBM APL2 (and unless
      ⍝ STRICT_IBM_APL2_FORMATTING), unscaled real numbers are aligned at
      ⍝ their decimal points; other items are right-aligned.
      ⍝
      ⎕PP←5
      3 1⍴600 (⊂1 2) 4.2E¯9
    600 
   1 2  
 4.2E¯9 



      4 1⍴1.5 22.25 333 (⊂4 5)
   1.5  
  22.25 
 333    
   4 5  



      3 1⍴'X' 8E6J4.2E5 3
        X
8E6J4.2E5
        3



      3 1⍴1J2 'X' 10.5
 1J2
   X
10.5



